  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Write $\\frac{3{x}^{6}+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x}$ in the form $a+\\frac{bx+c}{3{x}^{6}+2x},$ where $a\\ne 0.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$3{x}^{6}+8$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\" align=\"center\">$=$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\" align=\"center\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}} \n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$3{x}^{6}+2x$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$3{x}^{6}+2x$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "First, we add and subtract $2x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{6}+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x}\\,=\\,\\frac{3{x}^{6}+2x-2x+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{6}+2x-2x+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{6}+2x}{3{x}^{4}+2x}+\\frac{-2x+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-2x+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
